  <article class="container-article py-12 md:py-16">
    <Byline publishedDate="2026-03-16" />

    <div class="bg-secondary/40 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4 mb-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground mb-1">Direct Answer</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">At 6'6", the Steelcase Leap Plus is the only mainstream ergonomic chair that can clear the seat height bar, and only when ordered with the optional 5" cylinder that reaches 22.5". Its standard cylinder stops at 19.5" and will not fit. The Gesture at 21" and the Aeron Size C at 20.5" both leave the seat too low, which angles the thighs upward and drives the seat edge into the underside of the thigh. If the Leap Plus still does not fit, the next step is commercial-grade or custom seating rather than another mainstream chair.</p>
